# Rust build artifacts (Cargo.lock IS committed)
/target/

# turbovec / fastembed downloaded model cache (from the turbovec feature's tests)
/.fastembed_cache/

# Local event store / graph / scratch (runtime state; .rigger/workflow.yml IS committed)
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
.rigger/cache/
# Persisted turbovec grounding index (embeddings + the id->Ref map): per-machine
# derived data rebuilt from the tree, large + binary, never committed.
.rigger/grounding/
# The `rigger step` serialization lock (fs2 flock target): runtime-only, per-machine.
.rigger/step.lock
# The always-on dash's discoverability breadcrumbs (spec 39): the serving URL and the
# port+pid marker, rewritten on every run. Runtime-only, per-machine, never committed -
# left tracked they get swept into unit commits and collide with the live dash's rewrites
# when the conductor merges (the untracked-file-would-be-overwritten merge abort). Same
# reasoning covers dash.attempt (spec 69 round 8): the current run-id a step path last
# attempted a dash ensure for, rewritten on every step.
.rigger/dash.url
.rigger/dash.marker
.rigger/dash.attempt
# Persisted symbol index (spec 15): a rebuildable projection of the tree, per-machine
# derived data, never committed.
.rigger/symbols/
# Distilled playbook pool (spec 13, unit 7): a rebuildable projection of the log
# (`rigger playbooks --rebuild`), derived per-machine, never hand-edited state.
.rigger/playbooks/

# Node deps for the workflow shim (shim/package-lock.json IS committed)
shim/node_modules/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude
.rigger/shim
# The run's transient scratch root: unit/review worktrees + their build dirs
# (defaults.workdir / RIGGER_TMPDIR override the location; Gap 14)
.rigger/tmp
.rigger/store.conn

# The mutation-efficacy step's per-unit diff (rust-engineer.md: `git diff <BASE> --
# '*.rs' > unit.diff`), written at the worktree root as scratch input to
# `cargo mutants --in-diff`. Never a Done-when deliverable - ignore it wherever it
# lands so it can never be swept into a unit's commit again.
/unit.diff

# cargo-mutants' own output directory - and its `.old`-suffixed rotation, which
# cargo-mutants renames the previous run's directory to before writing a fresh
# one (spec 66 u66c3 fresh-r1: mutants.out.old/ leaked into a unit commit as
# 27 files / 22236 lines, the same scratch-leak class as /unit.diff above).
# Glob covers both today and any future cargo-mutants rotation suffix so this
# class cannot recur a third time in a different shape.
mutants.out*/
